       "PRINCIPLE_MULTIPLE_REPRESENTATIONS"
      ],
      "rationale": "A dot plot shows each data value, so the student can count values and find the median by counting in from each end. Some numbers on the scale have no dots, so the median is not just the middle of the scale.",
      "misconceptions": [
       "Taking the middle number on the scale as the median."
      ],
      "references": [
       "Common Core Standards Writing Team (2011), Progressions for Statistics and Probability, 6-8"
      ]
